From 8eb7d7071701177b822039a7b8a594102555f23d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (rhoai3 Stage 080)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:41:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): review handoff is terminal in the stop guard

The turn-end stop guard (agent/kanban_stop.py) treated only kanban_complete
and kanban_block as terminal, gated on the inherited HERMES_KANBAN_TASK env
var alone, and its nudge asserted the task "is still `running`" without
reading the board. A worker that correctly handed its card off with
kanban_request_review (or a reviewer that called kanban_request_changes) was
nudged up to twice to "call kanban_complete ... or kanban_block", steering it
to close or re-handle a card that was already under review. Delegated
children and in-process cron runs, which inherit the env var but own no
task, were nudged too.

- _TERMINAL_KANBAN_TOOLS now includes kanban_request_review and
  kanban_request_changes.
- kanban_stop_nudge_enabled() resolves identity through the new
  agent/delegation_context.py owned_kanban_task(): the nudge fires only for
  the dispatcher-owned worker, never for delegate_task children or
  non-dispatcher-owned (cron) contexts.
- The nudge no longer claims the card's status; it states that this session
  made no terminal board call and names every legal worker exit.
- The conversation-loop call site comment/status text and the worker-facing
  orchestrator-only refusal in tools/kanban_tools.py list the same exits.

A worker that makes no terminal call is still nudged (bounded, unchanged).

Backport of upstream NousResearch/hermes-agent commits:
  2bd0f1c59e5975676abe466bb06a0dc9da40326b fix(kanban): scope the stop nudge to the dispatcher-owned worker
  474db5363aac83a8395466584013264032ccc613 fix: kanban guidance and stop nudge resolve worker identity through one helper (owned_kanban_task + kanban_stop only)
  42500bf0cba4e2642a8f4f90db9fec593c1eedb8 fix(kanban): treat review-handoff tools as terminal in the stop guard
  41fe679d96ee640ae35beaca264b2fba70c3eb5a fix(kanban): stop-guard nudge names every worker exit; sync terminal-tool copies (stop-guard text only)

Tests: upstream test_kanban_stop.py cases for these commits, plus a
previous-tool -> nudge reproduction table (rhoai3 Stage 080 patch 0013).
